> From *The Runner's World Vegetarian Cookbook* ("Smoky Squash Flatbread with Balsamic Glaze"), as annotated — handwritten notes are the working method. Prefer the name Pumpkin Pizza. See `transcription-reviews/pumpkin-pizza.md` for photo review.

== Sauce ==

In a #small bowl{}, combine @pumpkin puree{15%oz}(1 can; or 12 oz thawed frozen winter squash puree), @Parmesan cheese{1/2%cup}(grated; pecorino also works), @garlic{2%cloves}(minced — skip if using garlic naan), @smoked paprika{3/4%tsp}(or regular paprika), @ground cumin{1/2%tsp}, @ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp}, @salt{1/4%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}. Stir until well combined. Set aside.

== Toppings & glaze ==

Trim stems from @Brussels sprouts{3/4%lb}. Shred in a #food processor{} with the shredding disk, or halve and thinly slice with a #knife{}. Toss with @extra-virgin olive oil{1%tbsp}.

In a #small saucepan{}, combine @balsamic vinegar{1/2%cup} and @light brown sugar{2%tsp}(firmly packed). Simmer over medium heat about ~{6%minutes}, until syrupy and reduced to about 2 tablespoons. Set aside.

== Assemble & cook (preferred) ==

Prep all components first, then assemble and toast one pizza at a time as you eat.

Use @naan{4}(Trader Joe's works well; garlic naan lets you skip the minced garlic in the sauce). Spread squash/pumpkin sauce over each, leaving about a 1/2-inch border. Top with the shredded Brussels sprouts, @goat cheese{1/4%cup}(crumbled, ~1 oz), and @hazelnuts{1/4%cup}(chopped, ~1 oz).

Heat on a #skillet{}, covered, over medium-low heat, with no oil — mostly it just needs to be toasty and warm. Drizzle with the balsamic glaze to serve.

== Oven option (printed method) ==

Preheat the #oven{} to 400°F. Line two #baking sheets{} with parchment or foil. Assemble all four flatbreads, bake about ~{10%minutes} until the crust is golden and the cheese begins to melt, then drizzle with glaze.
